        "title": "Understanding Mean Squared Error",
        "text": "The Mean Squared Error (MSE) is a measure of how well a model predicts the actual data. It is calculated by taking the average of the squares of the differences between the predicted values and the actual values. Can you express this in terms of $$y_i$$ and hat{y}_i?",
